          "selected": true
        },
        {
          "display_name": "DeepSeek",
          "execution_status": "SUCCESS",
          "provider": "deepseek",
          "rank": 2,
          "reason": "Fiscal Q1 beat-and-raise: EPS of $1.39 topped the $1.35 consensus on ~10.9% revenue growth and a record 51.5% gross margin, driven by volume rather than price. Truist lifted its target to $230 (Buy), and shares reversed the post-earnings dip to close +2.97% at $197.68, suggesting accumulation.",
          "risk": "At roughly 36x forward earnings, the multiple is exposed if hot inflation and rate fears persist and de-rate quality compounders; a broad pullback could outweigh the beat-and-raise.",
